+
+**Separate learning evidence from generation:** Tester corrections, rejected suggestions, original case versions, before/after expected observations, reviewer rationale and genuine execution outcomes are append-only attributable learning evidence independent of regenerated candidates. Regeneration, deduplication, case replacement, Skill rollback or model switch must not erase or relabel that history. A correction may produce a proposal, but only the existing exact human review and separate activation process can change the effective guidance. A candidate's performance must be assessed against independent outcomes rather than its own regenerated examples.
+
+**Authority and scope:** Normative precedence is determined by the actual approved owner and applicable jurisdiction/effective scope, not by an artifact type's name alone. A manual cannot override a binding policy; neither may an analyst assume every item named Policy is binding or applicable. AI interpretation, causal hypotheses, optional statistical prediction and deterministic traversal are distinct mechanisms and may be introduced incrementally. Insufficient labels, absent capability or an unjustified learning need supports a manual/deterministic/no-prediction outcome. Preserve every real attempt and declared aggregation grain; do not conflate relationship multiplicity with observations or predictions with confirmed defects.
